{"raw": {"https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/WTAMU_External/job/Canyon-TX/Associate-Professor-of-Educational-Leadership_R-097925-1": {"title": "Associate/Professor of Educational Leadership", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\nJob Title Associate/Professor of Educational Leadership Agency West Texas A&M University Department Education Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Canyon, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description NOTICE - All posted positions are subject to budget approval. \u00a0 \u00a0 Job Summary: \u00a0 West Texas A&M University (WTAMU), a Member of the Texas A&M University System, invites applications for one, and possibly two tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor positions, subject to budget approval, in the Doctor of Education (Ed.D.) in Educational Leadership program. These are full-time, 11-month appointments beginning January 1, 2027, or September 1, 2027, with competitive salaries and comprehensive benefits packages, commensurate with qualifications and experience. \u00a0 The Doctor of Education (Ed.D.) in Educational Leadership degree program at WTAMU is a fully online degree program emphasizing leadership in rural education at primary, secondary, post-secondary, and professional levels. The program operates on a cohort model, admitting one student cohort each calendar year. Students may select to pursue one of three pathways of study in the program that will advance their personal and professional goals. The pathways of study include EC-12 Educational Leadership in which the student may earn the Texas Superintendent Certificate, Higher Education Leadership , and Educational Business and Finance Leadership . The curriculum for each pathway requires the completion of 60 semester credit hours (SCHs) of coursework, inclusive of 48 SCHs of content-related coursework and 12 SCHs dedicated to writing and research. Options for specialized, advanced credentials and certificates are offered for those who elect to pursue them. \u00a0 A scholarly delivery requirement replaces a traditional dissertation. The scholarly delivery is comprised of a qualifying examination and the production of one written scholarly deliverable that is a publishable empirical research study in the field of educational leadership or a related field. The scholarly deliverable is the outcome of the doctoral student\u2019s empirical research conducted under the direction of a doctoral scholarly delivery committee. \u00a0 Work Performed: \u00a0 Teach doctoral-level courses in a fully online Ed.D. program Mentor and advise doctoral students, including supervision of empirical research Participate in the review of student progress including the qualifying examination Maintain an active research agenda with evidence of ongoing scholarly productivity Contribute to doctoral program development, assessment, and continuous improvement Participate in shared governance and program administration consistent with rank Engage in developing and implementing service opportunities consistent with the mission of the program, department, and college Weekly In-Person, On-campus (Canyon and/or Amarillo, Texas) office hours and engagement are required \u00a0 Necessary Qualifications: \u00a0 \u00a0 Terminal degree (Ed.D. or Ph.D.) in Educational Leadership or a closely related field Minimum of five (5) years of professional experience in EC\u201312 or higher education leadership positions or related leadership contexts that may include business and finance Demonstrated commitment to excellence in teaching, research, and service Evidence of an active research agenda and scholarly productivity appropriate to rank Demonstrated strong work ethic and commitment to doctoral education Proven ability to effectively mentor doctoral students, particularly in empirical research Demonstrated strong instructional effectiveness in fully online learning environments \u00a0 Preferred Qualifications: \u00a0 Previous instructional effectiveness in doctoral level content courses Previous service as Chair of scholarly delivery committees (e.g., dissertation or doctoral research committees) Experience working in rural educational contexts Experience or expertise in teaching the ethical use of Artificial Intelligence as it relates to research design, analysis, and scholarly writing Experience providing effective administrative leadership within a doctoral program Certified Texas superintendent \u00a0 Applicant Instructions: \u00a0 We require the following: \u00a0 Letter of interest or cover letter Curriculum Vitae Portfolio of creative work (where applicable) Personal statement to include philosophy and plans for research, teaching and service, as applicable Samples of unpublished works or works in progress (where applicable) Unofficial Transcripts (Official transcripts are expected to be submitted promptly by the successful candidate) Three professional references \u00a0 Please attach all documents in the attachment box at the bottom of the \u201cMy Experience\u201d page before continuing through the application.\u00a0 Please use the \u201cUpload\u201d button to add each document individually. All revisions must be made prior to application submission.\u00a0 If you need assistance with uploading documents, please contact WTAMU Human Resources at hr@wtamu.edu . \u00a0 Texas law requires that males age 18 through 25 be properly registered with the Selective Service System in order to be eligible for employment. \u00a0 All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution\u2019s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution\u2019s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer. The A&M System strives to maintain a competitive, high-quality benefit package to support the health and wellness needs of our workforce. This includes comprehensive health and welfare insurance plans, additional health and lifestyle programs, and optional retirement savings opportunities. Eligible employees will have access to paid leave programs in addition to 13-15 paid holidays each year. For more information regarding the benefit package go to: West Texas A&M University: Human Resources Benefits \u00a0 All applicants must attest they are not employed by and do not have any connection or continuous connections to any government entity or political apparatus of a country listed in 15 C.F.R. \u00a7 791.4 . Due to budgetary reasons, West Texas A&M University will not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and maintain work authorization throughout the employment term. \u00a0 For additional questions or information regarding this position, please contact: \u00a0 Search Committee Chair: \u00a0Dr. Betty Coneway Department: Education\u00a0 Phone:806-651-2664 Email: bconeway@wtamu.edu All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution\u2019s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution\u2019s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."}, "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/WTAMU_External/job/Canyon-TX/Assistant-Professor-Instructor-of-Media-Communication_R-097500-1": {"title": "Assistant Professor/Instructor of Media Communication", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-05\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Professor/Instructor of Media Communication Agency West Texas A&M University Department Communication Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Canyon, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description NOTICE - All posted positions are subject to budget approval. \u00a0 \u00a0 Job Summary: \u00a0 The Department of Communication at West Texas A&M University invites applications for an Assistant Professor (tenure-track) or Instructor (non-tenure-track) in Media Communication. The position requires excellence in teaching and professional service; tenure-track candidates would also have research expectations. A qualified applicant should have an established record of successfully teaching undergraduate media communication courses. Candidate may begin employment in either January or August 2027, depending on candidate qualifications and department needs. Work Performed: \u00a0 Teaching undergraduate courses in the areas of media communication, media trends, news production, basic video, and similar courses. Leading students, possibly in the Prairie News or the Sports Broadcasting practicum, which includes some travel. Teaching load is dependent on entering rank. Participating actively in discipline-specific professional associations and conferences (e.g., BEA, AEJMC) to maintain current knowledge of the field. Remaining up-to-date through scholarly research for tenure-track applicants. Rank of assistant professor requires regular production of peer-reviewed, scholarly conference presentations and journal publications. Supporting the department, college, and university through regular professional service and community outreach. \u00a0 Necessary Qualifications: \u00a0 Candidate must have a Master of Arts in Media Communication or Mass Communication (or a master\u2019s degree in a related course of study). To be considered for the tenure-track rank of assistant professor, candidates must have a Ph.D. in hand at the time of the contract. Candidate must demonstrate high-quality teaching experience in media communication. Candidate must have at least 2 years of professional, media-industry experience. Candidate must demonstrate the ability to develop and teach traditional and web-based courses with excellence. Candidate should have strong leadership and interpersonal communication skills, initiative, and the ability to excel in a student-centered environment. \u00a0 Preferred Qualifications: \u00a0 Experience advising and mentoring students. Experience in news production or broadcasting sporting events. Ph.D. in Media Communication or related field. \u00a0 \u00a0 Applicant Instructions: \u00a0 We require the following: \u00a0 Letter of interest or cover letter Curriculum Vitae Portfolio of creative work (where applicable) Personal statement to include teaching philosophy and plans for teaching and service; any tenure-track applicants should also address their plans for research, in addition to their teaching philosophy and plans for teaching and service Samples of unpublished works or works in progress (tenure-track applicants) Unofficial Transcripts (Official transcripts are expected to be submitted promptly by the successful candidate) List of three professional references \u00a0 Please attach all documents in the attachment box at the bottom of the \u201cMy Experience\u201d page before continuing through the application.\u00a0 Please use the \u201cUpload\u201d button to add each document individually. All revisions must be made prior to application submission.\u00a0 If you need assistance with uploading documents, please contact WTAMU Human Resources at hr@wtamu.edu . \u00a0 Texas law requires that males age 18 through 25 be properly registered with the Selective Service System in order to be eligible for employment. \u00a0 All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution\u2019s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution\u2019s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer. The A&M System strives to maintain a competitive, high-quality benefit package to support the health and wellness needs of our workforce. This includes comprehensive health and welfare insurance plans, additional health and lifestyle programs, and optional retirement savings opportunities. Eligible employees will have access to paid leave programs in addition to 13-15 paid holidays each year. For more information regarding the benefit package go to: West Texas A&M University: Human Resources Benefits \u00a0 All applicants must attest they are not employed by and do not have any connection or continuous connections to any government entity or political apparatus of a country listed in 15 C.F.R. \u00a7 791.4 . Due to budgetary reasons, West Texas A&M University will not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and maintain work authorization throughout the employment term. \u00a0 For additional questions or information regarding this position, please contact: \u00a0 Search Committee Chair:\u00a0 Dr. Emily Kinsky Department:\u00a0 Communication Phone: 806-651-2800 Email: ekinsky@wtamu.edu All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution\u2019s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution\u2019s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."}, "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/WTAMU_External/job/Canyon-TX/Assistant-Professor-of-Music-Therapy_R-097683-1": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Music Therapy", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-02\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Professor of Music Therapy Agency West Texas A&M University Department Music Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Canyon, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description NOTICE - All posted positions are subject to budget approval. \u00a0 \u00a0 Job Summary: \u00a0 Administer Music Therapy program; Teach Music Therapy courses, plus possible courses in a secondary area such as Music Theory or Music Education, depending on qualifications and experience.\u00a0 \u00a0 Work Performed:\u00a0 \u00a0 The position primarily includes teaching Music Therapy at the undergraduate level, administration of the clinical experience component for students, and other related courses. Additional responsibilities will depend on the candidate's interests and qualifications, including but not limited to, vocal or instrumental performance, conducting, and music theory. Maintain active program of research and publication. Serve as requested on school, college, and university committees and in leadership positions in community and professional organizations. \u00a0 Necessary Qualifications: \u00a0 The qualified candidate will have a Doctorate (PhD, EdD or DMA) in music therapy or related field; hold the MT-BC (Music Therapist-Board Certified) credential; holds a master\u2019s degree in music therapy or related area, with a minimum of transcripted graduate credits equivalent to 12 semester hours or the equivalent of graduate credits in music therapy beyond the undergraduate equivalency requirements; and has at least three years of full-time clinical experience in music therapy or its equivalent in part-time work. The candidate must meet the minimum qualification standards to serve as an undergraduate faculty member as outlined by the American Music Therapy Association (AMTA) found in Section 6.0 of the AMTA document Standards for Education and Clinical Training. \u00a0 The ability to creatively engage students in the classroom and to teach effectively online and in hybrid classes will be expected. The candidate will demonstrate knowledge of music therapy research and provide evidence of successful publication of research and scholarship. Active participation in professional organizations will also be expected. The candidate will also have the ability to teach and clinically supervise undergraduate students and the ability to organize and administer an undergraduate music therapy program. \u00a0 Preferred Qualifications: \u00a0 At least two years of previous college-level teaching is preferred. \u00a0 Applicant Instructions: \u00a0 We require the following: \u00a0 Letter of interest or cover letter Curriculum Vitae Personal statement to include philosophy and plans for research, teaching and service, as applicable Statement of personal educational philosophy and pedagogical practices. Unofficial Transcripts (Official transcripts are expected to be submitted promptly by the successful candidate)\u00a0 Three professional references \u00a0 Please attach all documents in the attachment box at the bottom of the \u201cMy Experience\u201d page before continuing through the application.\u00a0 Please use the \u201cUpload\u201d button to add each document individually. All revisions must be made prior to application submission.\u00a0 If you need assistance with uploading documents, please contact WTAMU Human Resources at hr@wtamu.edu . \u00a0 Texas law requires that males age 18 through 25 be properly registered with the Selective Service System in order to be eligible for employment. \u00a0 All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution\u2019s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution\u2019s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer. The A&M System strives to maintain a competitive, high-quality benefit package to support the health and wellness needs of our workforce. This includes comprehensive health and welfare insurance plans, additional health and lifestyle programs, and optional retirement savings opportunities. Eligible employees will have access to paid leave programs in addition to 13-15 paid holidays each year. For more information regarding the benefit package go to: West Texas A&M University: Human Resources Benefits \u00a0 All applicants must attest they are not employed by and do not have any connection or continuous connections to any government entity or political apparatus of a country listed in 15 C.F.R. \u00a7 791.4 . Due to budgetary reasons, West Texas A&M University will not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and maintain work authorization throughout the employment term. \u00a0 For additional questions or information regarding this position, please contact: \u00a0 Search Committee Chair: \u00a0Sarah Rushing Department:\u00a0 Music Phone: 806-651-2852 Email: srushing@wtamu.edu All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution\u2019s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution\u2019s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."}, "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/WTAMU_External/job/Canyon-TX/Director-of-Forensics_R-097502-1": {"title": "Director of Forensics", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-02\nFull time\n\nJob Title Director of Forensics Agency West Texas A&M University Department Communication Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Canyon, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description NOTICE - All posted positions are subject to budget approval. \u00a0 Candidate may begin employment in either January or August 2027, depending on candidate qualifications and department needs. \u00a0 \u00a0 Job Summary: \u00a0 Director of Forensics at rank of Instructor (with a master\u2019s degree) or Assistant Professor (with a Ph.D.) \u00a0 Work Performed: \u00a0 Directing and coaching the forensics team, which includes planning competitions, budgeting and managing expenses, travel, and other responsibilities related to team activity. Teaching undergraduate courses in the department, such as public speaking, interpersonal communication, argumentation and debate, small group communication, and organizational communication. Teaching load is dependent on entering rank with direction and coaching of forensics team, including travel, expected as part of the load. Candidates must have a Ph.D. at the time of the contract to be considered for rank of assistant professor. Actively participating in discipline-specific professional associations (e.g., NCA, SSCA, ICA) and remaining updated with scholarly research. Rank of assistant professor requires regular production of peer-reviewed and scholarly conference presentations and journal publications. Supporting the department, college, and university through regular professional service and community outreach. Qualified applicants might also teach graduate courses and be expected to help graduate students work toward completion of thesis and non-thesis options as an advisor or a committee member. \u00a0 Necessary Qualifications: \u00a0 Candidate must have a Master of Arts in Communication (or master's degree in a related course of study) or a Juris Doctorate. Candidate must demonstrate quality teaching experience in debate, oratory, oral interpretation, and basic speech courses. Candidate must demonstrate active involvement and experience in hosting speech and debate events, managing and coaching a competitive speech and debate team. Candidate must demonstrate the ability to develop and teach quality traditional, hybrid, and web-based courses. Candidate should have strong leadership and interpersonal communication skills, initiative, and the ability to excel in a student-centered environment. \u00a0 Preferred Qualifications: \u00a0 Experience advising and mentoring students. Experience managing UIL academic events. Demonstrated ability to teach graduate-level courses. Ph.D. in Communication or a related field. \u00a0 Applicant Instructions: \u00a0 We require the following: \u00a0 Letter of interest or cover letter Curriculum Vitae Portfolio of creative work (where applicable) Personal statement to include teaching philosophy and plans for teaching and service; any tenure-track applicants should also address their plans for research, in addition to their teaching philosophy and plans for teaching and service Samples of unpublished works or works in progress (where applicable) Unofficial Transcripts (Official transcripts are expected to be submitted promptly by the successful candidate) List of three professional references \u00a0 Please attach all documents in the attachment box at the bottom of the \u201cMy Experience\u201d page before continuing through the application.\u00a0 Please use the \u201cUpload\u201d button to add each document individually. All revisions must be made prior to application submission.\u00a0 If you need assistance with uploading documents, please contact WTAMU Human Resources at hr@wtamu.edu . \u00a0 Texas law requires that males age 18 through 25 be properly registered with the Selective Service System in order to be eligible for employment. \u00a0 All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution\u2019s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution\u2019s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer. The A&M System strives to maintain a competitive, high-quality benefit package to support the health and wellness needs of our workforce. This includes comprehensive health and welfare insurance plans, additional health and lifestyle programs, and optional retirement savings opportunities. Eligible employees will have access to paid leave programs in addition to 13-15 paid holidays each year. For more information regarding the benefit package go to: West Texas A&M University: Human Resources Benefits \u00a0 All applicants must attest they are not employed by and do not have any connection or continuous connections to any government entity or political apparatus of a country listed in 15 C.F.R. \u00a7 791.4 . Due to budgetary reasons, West Texas A&M University will not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and maintain work authorization throughout the employment term. \u00a0 For additional questions or information regarding this position, please contact: \u00a0 Search Committee Chair:\u00a0 Dr. Emily Kinsky Department:\u00a0 Communication Phone: 806-651-2800 Email: ekinsky@wtamu.edu All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution\u2019s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution\u2019s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."}, "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/WTAMU_External/job/Canyon-TX/Assistant-Professor-of-Biology_R-082360": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Biology", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-21\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Professor of Biology Agency West Texas A&M University Department Life, Earth & Environmental Sciences Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Canyon, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description NOTICE - All posted positions are subject to budget approval. West Texas A&M University, a Member of The Texas A&M University System located in Canyon, Texas, invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Biology (Microbiologist) (65% teaching, 30% research, 5% service).\u00a0 This full time (9 month) position at West Texas A&M University will include responsibilities in teaching (minimum of 9 ACH/semester), research, and service supportive of the Life Science Programs.\u00a0 Teaching duties will include existing or new courses within the successful candidate's area of expertise at the undergraduate and graduate levels, particularly related to the area of microbiology.\u00a0 The successful candidate is expected to conduct research in the area of microbiology and be amendable to collaboration with other faculty on relevant projects; attract and secure extramural funding; publish in genuine peer reviewed journals; attend professional meetings; provide academic advisement to undergraduate and graduate students; engage students in research; and develop and deliver effective educational programs to the community. Work Performed: Teaching selected undergraduate and graduate courses, such as General Biology, Microbiology, and Applied Microbiology with the possibility of developing new courses based on candidate's experience and expertise. Developing a dynamic research program by attracting new grants and opportunities that would allow undergraduate and graduate student participation. Conducting professional service for the institution, academic field, and community. Recruiting students for the undergraduate and graduate programs in Life, Earth, & Environmental Sciences Advising students on matters of degree plans, course scheduling, and other academic matters, including advising students enrolled I the premedical and other preprofessional programs. Necessary Qualifications: An earned Ph.D. in Biology or related area from an accredited institution.\u00a0 ABD will not be considered. Demonstrated experience and excellence in teaching related to the courses listed above. Willingness to teach 9 adjusted contact hours (ACH) per semester. Competency in research, as evidenced by publications (full citations) in genuine peer-reviewed journals. Experience in seeking/obtaining funding (including documentation of awards and amounts). Excellent quantitative, computer, written, and oral communication skills. Preferred Qualifications: Experience in instruction and mentoring of student research. An interest in and ability to teach general biology and microbiology. A willingness, with associated relevant experience, to take a lead position in directing a pre-medical, and more generally, a pre-healthcare program directed toward advising and preparing students for placement in medical and other professional schools. Demonstrated experience in seeking/obtaining extramural funding (including documentation of awards and amounts). Demonstrated ability and skills in leadership, mentoring, and building teamwork. Experience in developing collaborative research with other scientists, research centers and/or agencies and organizations. Applicant Instructions: \u00a0 We require the following:\u00a0 Letter of interest or cover letter Curriculum Vitae Personal statement to include philosophy and plans for research, teaching and service, as applicable Unofficial Transcripts (Official transcripts are expected to be submitted promptly by the successful candidate) Three professional references Please attach all documents in the attachment box at the bottom of the \u201cMy Experience\u201d page before continuing through the application.\u00a0 Please use the \u201cUpload\u201d button to add each document individually. All revisions must be made prior to application submission.\u00a0 If you need assistance with uploading documents, please contact WTAMU Human Resources at hr@wtamu.edu . Texas law requires that males aged 18 through 25 be properly registered with the Selective Service System in order to be eligible for employment. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution\u2019s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution\u2019s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer. The A&M System strives to maintain a competitive, high-quality benefit package to support the health and wellness needs of our workforce. This includes comprehensive health and welfare insurance plans, additional health and lifestyle programs, and optional retirement savings opportunities. Eligible employees will have access to paid leave programs in addition to 13-15 paid holidays each year. For more information regarding the benefit package go to: West Texas A&M University: Human Resources Benefits For additional questions or information regarding this position, please contact: Search Committee Chair: Jason Yarbrough Department: Life, Earth, and Environmental Science Phone: (806) 651-8042 Email: jyarbrough@wtamu.edu All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution\u2019s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution\u2019s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."}, "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/WTAMU_External/job/Canyon-TX/Professor-and-Head-of-the-Department-of-Agricultural-Sciences_R-091519-1": {"title": "Professor and Head of the Department of Agricultural Sciences", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-08\nFull time\n\nJob Title Professor and Head of the Department of Agricultural Sciences Agency West Texas A&M University Department Dean, College of Agriculture and Natural Scieneces Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Canyon, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description NOTICE - All posted positions are subject to budget approval. Job Summary: West Texas A&M University, a Member of The Texas A&M University System, invites applications for the position of Professor and Head of the Department of Agricultural Sciences.\u00a0 The position is a twelve-month, tenured position that reports to the Dean of the Paul Engler College of Agriculture and Natural Sciences. WTAMU is a four-year academic institution of 9,000 students serving the Panhandle of Texas and portions of four adjacent states. This geographic region is noted for its agricultural production and related businesses. The Department offers baccalaureate degrees in Agribusiness; Agricultural Business and Economics; Agriculture, Agriculture Education; Agricultural Communication, Animal Science; Equine Industry and Business; and Plant, Soil, and Environmental Science. Master of Science (M.S.) degrees are offered in Animal Science; Plant, Soil, and Environmental Science, and Agriculture with emphases options in Agriculture Education, Agricultural Media and Communication, and Agricultural Business and Economics; as well as an online Masters of Agriculture (M.Ag.). Additionally, a Ph.D. program is offered in Systems Agriculture.\u00a0 There are 1,200 students enrolled in the Department including 100 graduate students. The Department has a dynamic team of 30 full-time tenure-track faculty, four full-time clinical faculty, six full-time instructors, as well as research specialists and facility managers. Furthermore, the Department encompasses facilities, which support the academic and research mission including animal units, laboratories, greenhouses, and farms, as well as a new state-of-the-art beef cattle feedlot currently under construction with a planned capacity of approximately 4,400 head. Application review will begin May 1st Work Performed:\u00a0 Provide academic leadership to faculty, staff, and students in the Department of Agricultural Sciences Lead efforts to recruit, mentor, and evaluate faculty and staff while promoting their professional growth to sustain excellence in teaching, research, and service. Provide fiscal and operational oversight of all of the research and educational programs within the Department of Agricultural Sciences. Lead the development and implementation of academic programs that recruit, support, and graduate undergraduate and graduate students prepared to contribute meaningfully to the agricultural industry at the regional and broader levels. Collaborate with agricultural industry leaders to assess and address regional needs in teaching, research, and service. Coordinate with executive leadership to ensure the availability of resources required for successful program execution. Necessary Qualifications: Ph.D. in an agricultural discipline or closely related field offered by a University. Demonstrated commitment to excellence in teaching, research and service. Commitment to an interdisciplinary team approach to research, education and service. Interpersonal skills, vision and desire to establish working relationships both internally and outside of the University. Experience with managing federal, state, local, and grant accounting codes and funding structures. Proven ability to ensure efficient allocation of resources and adherence to fiscal guidelines.\u00a0 Evidence of administrative experience desired. Excellent computer, written, and oral communication skills. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled.\u00a0 Salary and benefits are competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience.\u00a0 Applicants should provide a letter of interest, curriculum vitae, official transcripts, and arrange for at least three letters of reference to be submitted online. Applicant Instructions: \u00a0 We require the following:\u00a0 Letter of interest or cover letter Curriculum Vitae Personal statement to include philosophy and plans for leadership vision Samples of unpublished works or works in progress (where applicable) Unofficial Transcripts (Official transcripts are expected to be submitted promptly by the successful candidate) Three professional references Please attach all documents in the attachment box at the bottom of the \u201cMy Experience\u201d page before continuing through the application.\u00a0 Please use the \u201cUpload\u201d button to add each document individually. All revisions must be made prior to application submission.\u00a0 If you need assistance with uploading documents, please contact WTAMU Human Resources at hr@wtamu.edu . Texas law requires that males age 18 through 25 be properly registered with the Selective Service System in order to be eligible for employment. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution\u2019s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution\u2019s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer. The A&M System strives to maintain a competitive, high-quality benefit package to support the health and wellness needs of our workforce. This includes comprehensive health and welfare insurance plans, additional health and lifestyle programs, and optional retirement savings opportunities. Eligible employees will have access to paid leave programs in addition to 13-15 paid holidays each year. For more information regarding the benefit package go to: West Texas A&M University: Human Resources Benefits Due to budgetary reasons, West Texas A&M University will not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and maintain work authorization throughout the employment term. All applicants must attest they are not employed by and do not have any connection or continuous connections to any government entity or political apparatus of a country listed in 15 C.F.R. \u00a7 791.4. For additional questions or information regarding this position, please contact: Search Committee Chair: Emilie Baker Department:\u00a0 Agricultural Sciences Phone: (806) 651-3586 Email: ebaker@wtamu.edu All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution\u2019s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution\u2019s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."}, "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/WTAMU_External/job/Canyon-TX/Assistant-Professor-of-Health-Sciences_R-095062-1": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Health Sciences", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-24\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Professor of Health Sciences Agency West Texas A&M University Department Sports And Exercise Science Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Canyon, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description NOTICE - All posted positions are subject to budget approval. Job Summary: The Health Science Faculty at West Texas A&M University is responsible for delivering high-quality instruction, supporting student success, and contributing to the growth and development of the Health Science Department. This position involves teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses, developing and revising curriculum, and engaging in service activities that support the mission of the university and the healthcare workforce needs of the Texas Panhandle. The instructor will provide engaging, evidence-based instruction in areas such as population health, healthcare systems, health promotion, and rural health, utilizing a variety of instructional modalities including face-to-face, hybrid, and online delivery. The role includes mentoring students, advising on academic and career pathways, and facilitating experiential learning opportunities such as internships, clinical placements, and community-based projects. In addition to teaching responsibilities, the Health Science Instructor will participate in program assessment, accreditation activities, and continuous quality improvement initiatives. The position requires collaboration with faculty, staff, and community partners to strengthen healthcare education pathways and expand workforce development efforts. The ideal candidate demonstrates a commitment to academic excellence, student-centered learning, and service to rural and underserved populations. This role supports the broader mission of West Texas A&M University by preparing graduates who are equipped to meet the evolving healthcare needs of the region and beyond. Work Performed: The Health Science Faculty at West Texas A&M University performs a broad range of teaching, service, and program development responsibilities that support the mission of the College of Nursing and Health Sciences and the University's commitment to preparing healthcare professionals who improve the health and well-being of the Texas Panhandle and beyond. The College emphasizes developing exemplary practitioners through education, research, service, outreach, and community partnerships. Primary responsibilities include planning, developing, and delivering undergraduate and graduate Health Science courses using evidence-based instructional practices in face-to-face, hybrid, and online learning environments. The instructor evaluates student learning outcomes, maintains academic records, provides academic advising and mentoring, and fosters an inclusive learning environment that promotes student engagement, retention, persistence, and graduation. Necessary Qualifications: Masters or Doctoral degree (PhD, DrPH, EdD, DNP, or related) in Health Sciences, Public Health, Healthcare Administration, or a closely related field from an accredited institution Demonstrated teaching effectiveness in undergraduate and/or graduate health science courses (face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online formats) Evidence of expertise in one or more relevant areas such as population health, rural health, healthcare systems, epidemiology, health promotion, or health policy Strong communication and interpersonal skills with the ability to engage diverse student populations Commitment to student success, mentorship, and experiential learning (internships, clinicals, or applied practice experiences) Ability to contribute to curriculum development, program assessment, and continuous quality improvement Demonstrated organizational and leadership skills to support program growth and community engagement Eligibility for appointment consistent with university and system policies Preferred Qualifications: Doctoral degree (PhD, DrPH, EdD, DNP, or related) in Health Sciences. Experience teaching in a rural-serving or regional university environment with a demonstrated record of scholarship, research, or creative activity appropriate to rank (publications, presentations, grant activity) Experience with accreditation processes (e.g., program review, outcomes assessment, compliance reporting) Established relationships or experience working with healthcare systems, public health agencies, or community organizations Experience securing or participating in grant-funded projects or workforce development initiatives Interdisciplinary collaboration experience across health-related programs Experience with student advising, retention initiatives, and career placement support Professional certification or licensure relevant to the discipline (e.g., CHES, MHA, RN, APRN, etc.), if applicable Applicant Instructions: \u00a0 We require the following:\u00a0 Letter of interest or cover letter Curriculum Vitae Portfolio of creative work (where applicable) Personal statement to include philosophy and plans for research, teaching and service, as applicable Samples of unpublished works or works in progress (where applicable) Unofficial Transcripts (Official transcripts are expected to be submitted promptly by the successful candidate) Three professional references Please attach all documents in the attachment box at the bottom of the \u201cMy Experience\u201d page before continuing through the application.\u00a0 Please use the \u201cUpload\u201d button to add each document individually. All revisions must be made prior to application submission.\u00a0 If you need assistance with uploading documents, please contact WTAMU Human Resources at hr@wtamu.edu . Texas law requires that males age 18 through 25 be properly registered with the Selective Service System in order to be eligible for employment. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution\u2019s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution\u2019s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer. The A&M System strives to maintain a competitive, high-quality benefit package to support the health and wellness needs of our workforce. This includes comprehensive health and welfare insurance plans, additional health and lifestyle programs, and optional retirement savings opportunities. Eligible employees will have access to paid leave programs in addition to 13-15 paid holidays each year. For more information regarding the benefit package go to: West Texas A&M University: Human Resources Benefits All applicants must attest they are not employed by and do not have any connection or continuous connections to any government entity or political apparatus of a country listed in 15 C.F.R. \u00a7 791.4. Due to budgetary reasons, West Texas A&M University will not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and maintain work authorization throughout the employment term. For additional questions or information regarding this position, please contact: Search Committee Chair: Michelle Kirksey\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Department: College of Nursing and Health Sciences Phone: (806) 651-2693 Email: mkirksey@wtamu.edu All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution\u2019s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution\u2019s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."}, "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/WTAMU_External/job/Canyon-TX/Assistant-Professor-of-Agricultural-Business-Economics_R-094880-1": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Agricultural Business/Economics", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-13\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Professor of Agricultural Business/Economics Agency West Texas A&M University Department Agricultural Sciences Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Canyon, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description NOTICE - All posted positions are subject to budget approval. Job Summary: West Texas A&M University, a member of The Texas A&M University System, invites applications for the position of Assistant Professor of Agricultural Business and Economics. This is a nine-month, tenure track position that reports to the Head of the Department of Agricultural Sciences. WTAMU is located in the Texas Panhandle, one of the largest cattle feeding areas in the world (6 million head annually), and one of the most prolific crop-producing areas in the world, (14 million acres of cultivated cropland), both of which are multi-billion dollars industries. The highest total value crops in the region are wheat, corn, ensilage, hay, sorghum and cotton. The position will focus on the various aspects of agricultural economics including but not limited to management, marketing, finance, policy, trade, and retail sales and will provide support to the current academic track to increase the enrollment at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. WTAMU is a four-year academic institution with more than 9,000 students including more than 1,150 students in the department granting Bachelor, Master of Science, Master of Agriculture, and Doctoral degrees. The department offers the following degrees related to the discipline: B.S. degree in Agribusiness, B.S. degree in Agricultural Business and Economics, M.S. in Agriculture with an emphasis in Agricultural Business and Economics, M.Ag, and a Ph.D. in Systems Agriculture. Work Performed:\u00a0 Teach a minimum of 9 hours per long semester. Teaching opportunities may include face-to-face and/or online formats. Contribute to a strong teaching program in the agricultural economics/agribusiness area with emphasis in at least one of the following areas: production and resource management, finance, international trade, policy, or management. Develop a research program in an area of agricultural economics/agribusiness. Secure extramural funding for research and scholarly activities. Advise M.S. and Ph.D. graduate students in various areas of Agricultural Business and Economics. Publish research findings and syntheses in refereed journals. Develop collaborative programs with scientists in other agencies, universities, and the agriculture industry. Develop strong industry relationships with agribusiness professionals in the region/state. Foster employment opportunities for both undergraduate and graduate students. Other duties as assigned. Necessary Qualifications: Ph.D. in Agricultural Economics, Economics, Agribusiness or closely related field Demonstrated commitment to excellence in teaching, research, and service Working knowledge and experience in crop and livestock industries Academic or industry experience beyond the Ph.D. is preferred Commitment to an interdisciplinary team approach to education and research Interpersonal skills, and desire to establish working relationships with external constituents in the allied agriculture industries Demonstrated experience in securing external funding and scholarly publication Excellent written and oral communication skills Applicant Instructions: \u00a0 We require the following:\u00a0 Letter of interest or cover letter Curriculum Vitae Portfolio of creative work (where applicable) Personal statement to include philosophy and plans for research, teaching and service, as applicable Samples of unpublished works or works in progress (where applicable) Unofficial Transcripts (Official transcripts are expected to be submitted promptly by the successful candidate) Three professional references Please attach all documents in the attachment box at the bottom of the \u201cMy Experience\u201d page before continuing through the application.\u00a0 Please use the \u201cUpload\u201d button to add each document individually. All revisions must be made prior to application submission.\u00a0 If you need assistance with uploading documents, please contact WTAMU Human Resources at hr@wtamu.edu . Texas law requires that males age 18 through 25 be properly registered with the Selective Service System in order to be eligible for employment. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution\u2019s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution\u2019s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer. The A&M System strives to maintain a competitive, high-quality benefit package to support the health and wellness needs of our workforce. This includes comprehensive health and welfare insurance plans, additional health and lifestyle programs, and optional retirement savings opportunities. Eligible employees will have access to paid leave programs in addition to 13-15 paid holidays each year. For more information regarding the benefit package go to: West Texas A&M University: Human Resources Benefits All applicants must attest they are not employed by and do not have any connection or continuous connections to any government entity or political apparatus of a country listed in 15 C.F.R. \u00a7 791.4. Due to budgetary reasons, West Texas A&M University will not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and maintain work authorization throughout the employment term. For additional questions or information regarding this position, please contact: Search Committee Chair:\u00a0 Dr. Bridget Guerrero Department:\u00a0 Agricultural Sciences Phone:\u00a0\u00a0 (806) 651-2614 Email:\u00a0\u00a0 bguerrero@wtamu.edu All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution\u2019s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution\u2019s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."}, "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/WTAMU_External/job/Canyon-TX/Assistant-Professor-of-Management_R-093555": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Management", "description": "Posted: 2026-05-26\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Professor of Management Agency West Texas A&M University Department Management, Marketing And General Business Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Canyon, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description NOTICE - All posted positions are subject to budget approval. Job Summary: The Assistant Professor of Management is responsible for teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in management and related disciplines, maintaining an active scholarly research agenda consistent with AACSB accreditation standards, and contributing to service activities within the department, college, university, and profession. The position requires a commitment to student engagement, instructional excellence in both face-to-face and online environments, and collaboration with faculty, staff, and external stakeholders. Areas of teaching may include Organizational Behavior, Human Resource Management, International Management, Strategic Management, Leadership, Hospitality Management, and Tourism. Faculty are also expected to support curriculum development, participate in assessment and accreditation activities, advise students, and contribute to the continued growth and strategic initiatives of the Paul and Virginia Engler College of Business . Work Performed:\u00a0 In a faculty position in management, the primary responsibilities include teaching undergraduate and/or graduate management courses, developing and updating course materials, advising and mentoring students, and assessing student learning outcomes. The faculty member will also conduct scholarly research in management and related fields, publish academic and professional work, and participate in departmental, college, and university service activities such as committees, curriculum development, assessment, and accreditation initiatives. Additional responsibilities include maintaining engagement with current management practices and emerging trends in areas such as leadership, organizational behavior, strategy, human resource management, hospitality management, and tourism. Faculty members may also collaborate with industry and community partners to support experiential learning, workforce development, and student career preparation. Necessary Qualifications: Applicants for the management faculty position must hold a doctorate (Ph.D. or DBA) in Management, Hospitality Management, Tourism Management, or a closely related field from an accredited institution. Candidates should demonstrate effectiveness in university-level teaching and possess a documented record of scholarly research or clear potential for research productivity in management or related areas. Preference will be given to candidates with the ability to teach in areas such as Organizational Behavior, Human Resource Management, Strategy, Leadership, Hospitality Management, and Tourism. Strong oral and written communication skills, collegiality, and the ability to work effectively with diverse students and colleagues are essential. Preferred Qualifications: Preferred qualifications include professional industry experience in hospitality management, tourism, lodging, event management, destination management, or related service industries. Preference will also be given to candidates with demonstrated industry engagement, applied managerial experience, or established connections with hospitality and tourism organizations that can support experiential learning, workforce development, and student career preparation. Applicant Instructions: \u00a0 We require the following:\u00a0 Letter of interest or cover letter Curriculum Vitae Portfolio of creative work (where applicable) Personal statement to include philosophy and plans for research, teaching and service, as applicable Samples of unpublished works or works in progress (where applicable) Unofficial Transcripts (Official transcripts are expected to be submitted promptly by the successful candidate) Three professional references Please attach all documents in the attachment box at the bottom of the \u201cMy Experience\u201d page before continuing through the application.\u00a0 Please use the \u201cUpload\u201d button to add each document individually. All revisions must be made prior to application submission.\u00a0 If you need assistance with uploading documents, please contact WTAMU Human Resources at hr@wtamu.edu . Texas law requires that males age 18 through 25 be properly registered with the Selective Service System in order to be eligible for employment. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution\u2019s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution\u2019s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer. The A&M System strives to maintain a competitive, high-quality benefit package to support the health and wellness needs of our workforce. This includes comprehensive health and welfare insurance plans, additional health and lifestyle programs, and optional retirement savings opportunities. Eligible employees will have access to paid leave programs in addition to 13-15 paid holidays each year. For more information regarding the benefit package go to: West Texas A&M University: Human Resources Benefits All applicants must attest they are not employed by and do not have any connection or continuous connections to any government entity or political apparatus of a country listed in 15 C.F.R. \u00a7 791.4. Due to budgetary reasons, West Texas A&M University will not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and maintain work authorization throughout the employment term. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution\u2019s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution\u2019s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."}, "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/WTAMU_External/job/Canyon-TX/Assistant-Professor-of-Counseling_R-093174-1": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Counseling", "description": "Posted: 2026-05-20\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Professor of Counseling Agency West Texas A&M University Department Education Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Canyon, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description NOTICE - All posted positions are subject to budget approval. Job Summary: West Texas A&M University\u2019s Department of Education invites applications for an assistant or associate professor of counseling position. This position is an exciting opportunity, designed to expand and enhance the capacity for rural behavioral health services. This initiative is in collaboration with professionals across a variety of fields and programs to ensure comprehensive service provision, including counseling, psychology, social work, nursing, etc. This unique position requires an individual that exhibits a passion for supervision, consultation, and training who will not only work collaboratively with the faculty of the Counseling program but will be eager to cooperate with other departments and external agencies across the Texas Panhandle Community to develop the Behavioral Health Workforce Initiative (BHWI) at West Texas A&M University. This position is an 11-month tenure-track position. Teaching responsibilities will be in the graduate online Counseling program. The successful candidate will maintain an active research and publication agenda, participate in program, departmental, college, and university committees, engage with professional counseling organizations, and willingly complete other duties as assigned.\u202f Work Performed:\u00a0 Coordinate clinical mental health services in collaboration with the mental/behavioral health initiative Develop and maintain community partnerships Collaborate with partner schools and community agencies Collaborate with university personnel responsible for BHWI program data collection and management Supervise and teach graduate practicum and internship supervision courses, which may include summer terms Work cooperatively with public/private schools and mental health agencies Recruit, admit, and advise master\u2019s level counseling students Maintain an active research and publication agenda Actively participate in program planning, review of comprehensive examinations, and university assessment requirements Engage in developing and implementing service opportunities consistent with the mission and vision of the program, department, and college Collaborate and meet regularly with counseling and college faculty Necessary Qualifications: Earned doctorate in Counselor Education Texas state licensure as Licensed Professional Counselor (LPC) or license eligible\u00a0 Evidenced scholarly activity or scholarly agenda in the field of Counseling\u00a0 Experience supervising counselors-in-training throughout practicum and internship Evidence of experience developing, implementing, and evaluating clinical procedures for counselors-in-training Preferred Qualifications: A doctoral degree in Counseling from a CACREP accredited program\u00a0 Specialized training in Counseling curriculum and online instruction development\u00a0 Demonstrated commitment to excellence in teaching, research, and service\u00a0 Minimum of two years of experience teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses in educator preparation courses in Counseling in a higher education setting (i.e., university or community college) Evidence of consultation and training in the mental health services\u00a0(school and community)\u00a0 Strong working knowledge and understanding of established professional code of ethics and best practices in Counseling Education Applicant Instructions: \u00a0 We require the following:\u00a0 Letter of interest or cover letter Curriculum Vitae Personal statement to include philosophy and plans for research, teaching and service, as applicable Samples of unpublished works or works in progress (where applicable) Unofficial Transcripts (Official transcripts must be submitted promptly by the successful candidate) Three professional references Please attach all documents in the attachment box at the bottom of the \u201cMy Experience\u201d page before continuing through the application.\u00a0 Please use the \u201cUpload\u201d button to add each document individually. All revisions must be made prior to application submission.\u00a0 If you need assistance with uploading documents, please contact WTAMU Human Resources at hr@wtamu.edu . Texas law requires that males age 18 through 25 be properly registered with the Selective Service System in order to be eligible for employment. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution\u2019s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution\u2019s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer. The A&M System strives to maintain a competitive, high-quality benefit package to support the health and wellness needs of our workforce. This includes comprehensive health and welfare insurance plans, additional health and lifestyle programs, and optional retirement savings opportunities. Eligible employees will have access to paid leave programs in addition to 13-15 paid holidays each year. For more information regarding the benefit package go to: West Texas A&M University: Human Resources Benefits All applicants must attest they are not employed by and do not have any connection or continuous connections to any government entity or political apparatus of a country listed in 15 C.F.R. \u00a7 791.4. Due to budgetary reasons, West Texas A&M University will not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and maintain work authorization throughout the employment term. For additional questions or information regarding this position, please contact: Search Committee Chair: Dr. Betty Coneway Department: Education Phone:806-651-2664 Email: bconeway@wtamu.edu All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution\u2019s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution\u2019s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."}, "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/WTAMU_External/job/Canyon-TX/Part-Time-Instructor-of-Biology_R-045805": {"title": "Part Time Instructor of Biology", "description": "Posted: 2026-04-13\nPart time\n\nJob Title Part Time Instructor of Biology Agency West Texas A&M University Department Life, Earth & Environmental Sciences Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Canyon, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description NOTICE - All posted positions are subject to budget approval. The A&M System strives to maintain a competitive, high-quality benefit package to support the health and wellness needs of our workforce. This includes comprehensive health and welfare insurance plans, additional health and lifestyle programs, and optional retirement savings opportunities. Eligible employees will have access to paid leave programs in addition to 13-15 paid holidays each year. For more information regarding the benefit package go to: West Texas A&M University: Human Resources Benefits The Department of Life, earth, & Environmental Sciences at West Texas A&M University seeks to establish a pool of qualified applicants for future, part-time appointments as teachers of biology courses. Description: Teach on to four sections of biology courses as needed by the department. Hold office hours and assist students as needed. Necessary Qualifications: A Master's Degree in Biology or related discipline and at least 18 graduate hours in biological sciences are required. Applicants must be available to teach courses on campus. Applicant Instructions: To be considered, applicants must include: Cover letter CV/Resume Three references Graduate transcripts Please attach all documents in the attachment box at the bottom of the \u201cMy Experience\u201d page before continuing through the application.\u00a0 Please use the \u201cUpload\u201d button to add each document individually. All revisions must be made prior to application submission.\u00a0 If you need assistance with uploading documents, please contact WTAMU Human Resources at hr@wtamu.edu . Texas law requires that males age 18 through 25 be properly registered with the Selective Service System in order to be eligible for employment. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution\u2019s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution\u2019s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer. The A&M System strives to maintain a competitive, high-quality benefit package to support the health and wellness needs of our workforce. This includes comprehensive health and welfare insurance plans, additional health and lifestyle programs, and optional retirement savings opportunities. Eligible employees will have access to paid leave programs in addition to 13-15 paid holidays each year. For more information regarding the benefit package go to: West Texas A&M University: Human Resources Benefits All applicants must attest they are not employed by and do not have any connection or continuous connections to any government entity or political apparatus of a country listed in 15 C.F.R. \u00a7 791.4. Due to budgetary reasons, West Texas A&M University will not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and maintain work authorization throughout the employment term. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution\u2019s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution\u2019s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."}, "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/WTAMU_External/job/Canyon-TX/Part-Time-Instructor-of-Chemistry_R-045792": {"title": "Part Time Instructor of Chemistry", "description": "Posted: 2026-04-13\nPart time\n\nJob Title Part Time Instructor of Chemistry Agency West Texas A&M University Department Department Of Chemistry And Physics0 Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Canyon, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description NOTICE - All posted positions are subject to budget approval. The A&M System strives to maintain a competitive, high-quality benefit package to support the health and wellness needs of our workforce. This includes comprehensive health and welfare insurance plans, additional health and lifestyle programs, and optional retirement savings opportunities. Eligible employees will have access to paid leave programs in addition to 13-15 paid holidays each year. For more information regarding the benefit package go to: West Texas A&M University: Human Resources Benefits The Department of Chemistry and Physics at West Texas A&M University seeks to establish a pool of qualified applicants for future, part-time appointments as instructor of chemistry. Responsibilities: Teach one to four sections of chemistry as needed by the department. Hold office hours and assist students as needed. Necessary Qualifications A Master's Degree in Chemistry or in a closely related field and at least 18 graduate hours in chemistry. Applicants must be available to teach courses on campus Applicant Instructions: To be considered, applicants must include: Cover Letter CV/Resume Three references Graduate transcripts Please attach all documents in the attachment box at the bottom of the \u201cMy Experience\u201d page before continuing through the application.\u00a0 Please use the \u201cUpload\u201d button to add each document individually. All revisions must be made prior to application submission.\u00a0 If you need assistance with uploading documents, please contact WTAMU Human Resources at hr@wtamu.edu . Texas law requires that males age 18 through 25 be properly registered with the Selective Service System in order to be eligible for employment. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution\u2019s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution\u2019s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer. The A&M System strives to maintain a competitive, high-quality benefit package to support the health and wellness needs of our workforce. This includes comprehensive health and welfare insurance plans, additional health and lifestyle programs, and optional retirement savings opportunities. Eligible employees will have access to paid leave programs in addition to 13-15 paid holidays each year. For more information regarding the benefit package go to: West Texas A&M University: Human Resources Benefits All applicants must attest they are not employed by and do not have any connection or continuous connections to any government entity or political apparatus of a country listed in 15 C.F.R. \u00a7 791.4. Due to budgetary reasons, West Texas A&M University will not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and maintain work authorization throughout the employment term. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution\u2019s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution\u2019s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."}, "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/WTAMU_External/job/Canyon-TX/Part-Time-Instructor-of-Dance_R-061853": {"title": "Part-Time Instructor of Dance", "description": "Posted: 2025-05-08\nPart time\n\nJob Title Part-Time Instructor of Dance Agency West Texas A&M University Department Art, Theatre & Dance Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Canyon, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description NOTICE - All posted positions are subject to budget approval. The A&M System strives to maintain a competitive, high-quality benefit package to support the health and wellness needs of our workforce. This includes comprehensive health and welfare insurance plans, additional health and lifestyle programs, and optional retirement savings opportunities. Eligible employees will have access to paid leave programs in addition to 13-15 paid holidays each year. For more information regarding the benefit package go to: West Texas A&M University: Human Resources Benefits Work Performed: The Part-Time Instructor of Dance will teach courses in support of a Bachelor of Fine Arts in Dance degree with both performing and education emphases, choreograph for faculty concerts, supervise student concerts, and assist with other program needs. Necessary Qualifications: Master's degree and at least 18 hours in content area Experience teaching ballet, modern dance, improvisation, and choreography. Preferred Qualifications: MA in Dance Experience teaching ballet, modern dance, improvisation, and choreography at the university level. Experience teaching theory courses online. Demonstrated ability to teach in other selected areas from: dance history, teaching methods, partnering (ballet or contemporary), jazz, tap, musical theatre dance, and somatics (prefer certification). Applicant Instructions: Please include the following with your application: Cover letter Resume Three references Please attach all documents in the attachment box at the bottom of the \u201cMy Experience\u201d page before continuing through the application.\u00a0 Please use the \u201cUpload\u201d button to add each document individually. All revisions must be made prior to application submission.\u00a0 If you need assistance with uploading documents, please contact WTAMU Human Resources at hr@wtamu.edu . Texas law requires all males aged 18 through 25 to be properly registered with the Selective Service System. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution\u2019s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution\u2019s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."}}, "rows": {"https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/WTAMU_External/job/Canyon-TX/Associate-Professor-of-Educational-Leadership_R-097925-1": {"school_id": 1372, "posting_url": "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/WTAMU_External/job/Canyon-TX/Associate-Professor-of-Educational-Leadership_R-097925-1", "job_title_in_post": "Associate/Professor of Educational Leadership", "position_type": "Full_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "Educational Leadership", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": "2026-10-12"}, "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/WTAMU_External/job/Canyon-TX/Assistant-Professor-Instructor-of-Media-Communication_R-097500-1": {"school_id": 1372, "posting_url": "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/WTAMU_External/job/Canyon-TX/Assistant-Professor-Instructor-of-Media-Communication_R-097500-1", "job_title_in_post": "Assistant Professor/Instructor of Media Communication", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "Department of Communication", "area_key_words": "Media Communication; news production", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": "2026-10-05"}, "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/WTAMU_External/job/Canyon-TX/Assistant-Professor-of-Music-Therapy_R-097683-1": {"school_id": 1372, "posting_url": "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/WTAMU_External/job/Canyon-TX/Assistant-Professor-of-Music-Therapy_R-097683-1", "job_tit